Each year, the Linux Foundation's Technical Advisory Board seeks an
organizing committee for the annual Linux Plumbers Conference.  That
process has now begun for the 2015 event, which will be held during the
week of August 17-21 in Seattle, Washington, alongside the LinuxCon North
America event.  This is your chance to put your stamp on one of our
community's most important gatherings.

Interested groups should have, at a minimum, an events coordinator, a
treasurer, and a chairperson.  This group must be able to take the
initiative to handle conference-specific details (including social events,
the miniconf program, and more) while working with the Linux Foundation to
ensure that logistics work smoothly.

The process for putting in an application to run the Linux Plumbers
Conference is documented here:

	   https://wiki.linuxfoundation.org/en/LPC

Applications should be in by October 31, 2014; the TAB then will
announce a decision by (at the latest) the end of November.

jon (for the LF TAB)
